==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|anelich}}, {{m|gmh|enlich|t=alike}}, from {{inh|de|goh||*analīh}} (attested in derivatives), a contraction of {{m|goh|anagilīh}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*anagalīkaz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*ana|t1=on}} + {{m|gem-pro|*galīkaz|t2=like}}, that is “almost identical”. Compare {{m+|de|angleichen}}. Cognate with {{cog|dum|aenlijck}}, {{cog|en|alike}}, {{cog|non|álíkr}}.

The contemporary form is possibly from a merger of {{m+|gmh||anelich}} with [[East Central German]] {{m|de|einlich}}, but it is uncertain whether the latter is from {{suffix|de|ein|t1=one|-lich|t2=-ly}} or merely an alteration of the former. The form may also have been reinforced by interpretation as {{suffix|de|Ahn|t1=ancestor|-lich}}; this noun is not related.

